{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/790293-mundane-weapon-damage-in-vtr-2nd-edition","id":790293,"title":"\"Mundane\" weapon damage in VtR 2nd Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-21T08:45:38-08:00","id":790293,"title":"\"Mundane\" weapon damage in VtR 2nd Edition","content":"I have a question I can't seem to find the answer to here on the forums.<br /> <br /> My group is switching over to the new rules for the first time so I am looking for a rules clarification: VtR 2nd Edition, under &quot;Injury and Healing&quot;, it says that Kindred take bashing damage from &quot;all mundane weapons&quot;. What constitutes a mundane weapon? I first assumed that meant all weapons other than firearms and supernatural attacks, but on the next page, the example for marking health boxes says Persephone is &quot;stabbed and takes a point of Lethal damage&quot; Is a knife/sword not mundane? Also, on of the FAQs say that Protean Claws would do bashing to a vampire. Are they not considered supernatural even though it comes from a discipline?<br /> <br /> thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10393-rbg96","name":"RBG96","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T08:55:07-08:00","id":790298,"title":"","content":"A mundane weapon is anything that doesn't mention that it does lethal to vampires. Knives, guns, claws, pretty much everything except protean 4 claws, cruac and theban sorcery rituals and werewolf teeth at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T08:58:40-08:00","id":790299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RBG96</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/790293-mundane-weapon-damage-in-vtr-2nd-edition#post790293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question I can't seem to find the answer to here on the forums.<br /> <br /> My group is switching over to the new rules for the first time so I am looking for a rules clarification: VtR 2nd Edition, under &quot;Injury and Healing&quot;, it says that Kindred take bashing damage from &quot;all mundane weapons&quot;. What constitutes a mundane weapon? I first assumed that meant all weapons other than firearms and supernatural attacks, but on the next page, the example for marking health boxes says Persephone is &quot;stabbed and takes a point of Lethal damage&quot; Is a knife/sword not mundane? Also, on of the FAQs say that Protean Claws would do bashing to a vampire. Are they not considered supernatural even though it comes from a discipline?<br /> <br /> thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>Persephone's a mortal. Which is understandably confusing, since it's the vampire book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T10:34:30-08:00","id":790341,"title":"","content":"It means nonmagical weapons. Knife does bashing, gun does bashing. Protean 2 claws do bashing because the magic is in the ability to grow animal claws, not in the claws themselves; Protean 4 can produce claws that deal lethal damage to vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T10:40:45-08:00","id":790344,"title":"","content":"Here's what David H. has to say on the matter:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/122291-uratha-teeth-and-claws?p=125207#post125207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it'd do aggravated to a human, it does lethal to a vampire.<br /> If it'd do lethal to a human, it does bashing to a vampire.<br /> If it's a direct damage power in a Vampire book, it does the damage suggested since we're referencing vampires primarily in that book.<br /> If the power makes a mundane weapon or cause of harm, downgrade it. Protean 2 is a good example.<br /> If the power makes a weapon, and we say it does X to vampires, it does X to vampires. Protean 4 is a good example.<br /> If someone in my games paid Experience for something to hurt vampires, it should hurt them. A Fighting Style that does aggravated should probably do aggravated, because of the investment involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T11:01:53-08:00","id":790354,"title":"","content":"I am sorry to hijack your thread, but this sort of relates. *I think* I read somewhere that the weapons from armory are 1E, so we are suppose to take 1 die off since it does auto damage now instead of dice. So would the sniper rifle that says +5 actually be a 4L? therefore, bashing?<br /> <br /> Would incendiary rounds do aggravated to a vampire or Lethal or bashing? I do not claim to be an ammo expert, I only know what wikipedia tells me.... Do they do actual fire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T11:03:43-08:00","id":790355,"title":"","content":"Beware the Barghest!<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://vignette2.wikia.nocookie.net/non-aliencreatures/images/b/bb/Barghest.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20101124062934\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T11:30:53-08:00","id":790369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/790293-mundane-weapon-damage-in-vtr-2nd-edition?p=790354#post790354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am sorry to hijack your thread, but this sort of relates. *I think* I read somewhere that the weapons from armory are 1E, so we are suppose to take 1 die off since it does auto damage now instead of dice. So would the sniper rifle that says +5 actually be a 4L? therefore, bashing?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/790293-mundane-weapon-damage-in-vtr-2nd-edition?p=790354#post790354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would incendiary rounds do aggravated to a vampire or Lethal or bashing? I do not claim to be an ammo expert, I only know what wikipedia tells me.... Do they do actual fire?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say the damage from the impact (the successes + weapon damage) would be bashing, and any damage from the subsequent explosion would follow the rules for explosives (I don't know them very well, since I've never had to deal with them in an actual game). Any fires caused by the explosion would do normal fire damage (which would be aggravated).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T11:33:04-08:00","id":790373,"title":"","content":"Dragon Breath rounds? Sure it causes Aggravated in my table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T11:45:25-08:00","id":790380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/790293-mundane-weapon-damage-in-vtr-2nd-edition?p=790373#post790373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon Breath rounds? Sure it causes Aggravated in my table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, dragon's breath definitely would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T12:20:26-08:00","id":790408,"title":"","content":"For reference:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/00/Dragonsbreath.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T12:37:59-08:00","id":790426,"title":"","content":"It may be important to note that Dragon's Breath rounds are, despite being incendiary completely atypical of incendiary ammunition.,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T13:51:10-08:00","id":790464,"title":"","content":"Sorry for my failure here. I dont know what Dragon Breath rounds are... I am talking like real life incendiary rounds. I thought they just had a chemical to go boom.. Which is not actual fire. just an explosive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T16:03:54-08:00","id":790550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/790293-mundane-weapon-damage-in-vtr-2nd-edition?p=790464#post790464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for my failure here. I dont know what Dragon Breath rounds are... I am talking like real life incendiary rounds. I thought they just had a chemical to go boom.. Which is not actual fire. just an explosive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon's Breath rounds are real. Most &quot;Incindeary&quot; rounds are, as you indicate, normal bullets that explode on or shortly after contact. Personally, I would handle them with the rules for explosives. Dragon's Breath rounds are a kind of shotgun ammunition that shoots huge jets of flames. The picture Ephsy posted above is an example of what that looks like. Personally, I would handle a shotgun loaded with Dragon's Breath like a flamethrower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T03:47:25-08:00","id":790787,"title":"","content":"There are three types of incindiary rounds: Dragon's breath basically turns your firearm into a flamethrower, there's the explosive kind (which we're talking about) and tracer rounds. As per Armory book, flamethrower rounds have 4L (fire damage) with a range of 75', and tracer rounds add +Wits/2 as an aiming bonus to medium bursts, +Wits to long bursts. <br /> <br /> The explosive kinds of incindiary rounds are interesting, because they're designed to explode upon impact, and not really set things on fire. Its been known to happen on occasion, but that's the exception and not the rule. From what I understand of 2e rules, with explosions, you just take the weapon damage in auto-successes in the range of the explosive. However, that's if you don't end up as the direct target of the explosion. For being the direct target? Actually, I'd probably just make the gun's damage rating aggravated damage there (and thus lethal damage to vamps). <br /> <br /> I don't know about any incindiary rounds designed to start fires upon hitting the target, but thermite bombs burn hot and small for long periods of time. Not even a vampire with Resilience 5 can survive one for the 10 minutes it takes to finish burning; its just a question of how long it takes. If there are rounds that can do the same thing, I would frankly ban them. Its an instant death sentence, which undermines a lot of the traditional themes of vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T08:55:20-08:00","id":790871,"title":"","content":"Awesome! Thanks so much guys. I really appreciate it and again sorry to hijack this thread!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}